Fixed. The bug was in `src/resources/storage.ts:25` — `clampToStorageCap` clamped `wood` and `stone` to the cap but returned `food` unmodified:

```js
food: resources.food,   // → food: Math.min(resources.food, cap),
```

That's why food stockpiled past the storage cap while wood and stone were correctly capped. Now food is clamped the same way every other resource is. I also removed the now-stale "BUG" comment and the stale "still-buggy food case" note in `utilizationOf`.

Verified: `npm test` (15 passed) and `npm run typecheck` both pass. `clampToStorageCap` is the single choke point for the cap in `src/sim/turn.ts:20`, so no other call path needed touching.


